      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While vitamin C can help maintain urinary health and may aid in flushing out minor stone fragments, taking extremely high doses (2500mg per day) of vitamin C in an attempt to clear out buildup is not the optimal approach for several reasons. High doses of vitamin C can put pressure on your kidneys, which may exacerbate existing kidney stone issues. Consult your doctor or a qualified healthcare professional for a personalized advice on managing your kidney stones and developing a safe detox plan.",
