      "content": "While vitamin C does have anti-inflammatory properties and is an antioxidant, the scientific evidence supporting its use as a detox tool to prevent or treat kidney stones is limited and inconclusive. Studies have shown variable results, and more research is needed to fully understand its effects on kidney stone formation. Additionally, taking high doses of vitamin C may have other unintended consequences, such as gastrointestinal side effects or interactions with certain medications.",
